<title>JAPAN: BOBSLEIGH-WORLD CUP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BOBSLEIGH-WORLD CUP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>NAGANO, Japan 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of a World Cup</p>
<p>four-man bobsleigh event on Tuesday:</p>
<p>1. USA I (Brian Shimer (Chip Minton, Randy Jones, Robert</p>
<p>Olesen) 1 minute, 45.75 seconds (first run 52.71 seconds, second</p>
<p>run 53.04 seconds)</p>
<p>2. Germany II (Dirk Wiese, Christoph Bartsch, Thorsten Weber,</p>
<p>Michael Liekmeier) 1:46.02 (52.99/53.03)</p>
<p>3. France I (Bruneo Mingeon, Emanuel Hostache, Eric Le</p>
<p>Chanony, Max Robert) 1:46.07 (52.77/53.30)</p>
<p>4. Switzerland II (Marcel Rohner, Markus Nuessli, Thomas</p>
<p>Schreiber, Roland Tanner) 1:46.10 (52.96/53.14)</p>
<p>5. Latvia I (Sandis Prusis, Egils Bojars, Adris Pluksna, Janis</p>
<p>Elsins) 1:46.11 (52.97/53.14)</p>
<p>6. Italy I (Guenther Huber, Antonio Tartaglia, Massimiliano</p>
<p>Rota, Marco Menchini) 1:46.15 (52.89/53.26)</p>
<p>7 equal. Germany I (Wolfgang Hoppe, Ulf Hielscher, Rene</p>
<p>Hannemann, Carsten Embach) 1:46.23 (52.96/53.27)</p>
<p>7 equal. Canada I (Pierre Lueders, Steve Wiseman, Dave</p>
<p>MacEachern, Jack Pyc) 1:46.23 (53.14/53.09)</p>
<p>9. USA II (Jim Herberich, Jason Dorsey, John Kasper, Garrett</p>
<p>Hines) 1:46.24 (52.90/53.34)</p>
<p>10. Austria I (Hubert Schoesser, Gerd Habermueller, Erwin</p>
<p>Arnold, Martin Schuetzenauer) 1:46.27 (53.15/53.12)</p>
<p>World Cup four-man standings after six of seven races:</p>
<p>  1. Marcel Rohner (Switzerland)	178 points</p>
<p>  2. Wolfgang Hoppe (Germany)	   168</p>
<p>  3. Dirk Wiese (Germany)		 167</p>
<p>  4. Guenther Huber (Italy)	     166</p>
<p>  5. Brian Shimer (U.S.)		  141</p>
<p>  6. Bruno Mingeon (France)	     135</p>
<p>  7. Hubert Schoesser (Austria)	 125</p>
<p>  8. Sandis Prusis (Latvia)	     124</p>
<p>  9. Jim Herberich (U.S.)		 121</p>
<p> 10. Harald Czudaj (Germany)	    119</p>
